post</a></i></div></p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>If you’re like me, over the years you’ll have had your todo lists
scattered over multiple programs and places. First a simple text file
with homebrewn format, then various Windows programs, then various
Linux GUI programs, then back to Notepad and joe/gedit/kate, then
various apps on cellphones, then pencil &#x26; paper (due to cellphones
keep getting lost/stolen), then some cloud apps, then todo.txt, then
finally org-mode. And if you’re anything like me or many others,
you’ll find that org-mode is <strong>it</strong>.  <div
align="right"><i>Stephen Haryanto in a <a href="http://blogs.perl.org/users/steven_haryanto/2011/03/orgparser.html">blog post</a></i></div></p>
</blockquote>
